WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.168
-We're back with Common,
everybody.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.370
You write about
your love of the Bulls.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.738
The Chicago Bulls.
You write about your love

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.273
of Michael Jordan.
I did not realize this.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.508
Michael Jordan
actually saw you play

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.078
in a celebrity all-star game.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.247
-Yes.
-In 2010.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.148
-Yes.
-And had some notes.

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.450
-Well, yeah.
Well, first of all,

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:22.188
I work hard to get into those
celebrity basketball games

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.823
because I love basketball.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.792
-And so many of my friends
are watching,

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.927
so I'm looking to show up
and do great.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.429
That year, I did great.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.165
Like, I really thought
I was going to get MVP,

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.533
and I ended up,
after the game,

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.936
going to Michael Jordan's
brand Jordan party

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:39.538
and he, you know, he said,
"Common, come here."

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.208
And I, you know,
gave him a little love.

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:46.045
And he said in my ear,
"Stick to rapping and acting."

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.547
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:51.250
I was like, "Mike, man,
I just killed it on the court."

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.419
But not to him. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.054
I will say,
I would have thought

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.322
that was a weird thing
to say to you

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.857
until I saw "The Last Dance."

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.558
Then, I'm like, no,
that's in line, right?

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.561
-[ Laughs ]
-Right?

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.196
He saw you as competition.
-Yeah. Yeah, exactly.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.597
-Now, I will say you did --

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.231
you said you thought you were
going to win the MVP --

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:08.968
10 years later, which again
speaks to how well you're aging.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.270
-Thank you.
-2020 celebrity game,

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.605
you did win the MVP.

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.308
Now, that's a real trophy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.409
That's a real trophy
right there.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.778
-Let me tell you.
Let me tell you.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.814
I've received some awards,
and I'm very grateful.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.416
But this was one
I was fighting for

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.817
for a while, man.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.688
And I flew home
with that MVP trophy,

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.489
and I tried to take
the Michael Jordan picture.

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:31.623
I wish I had that,

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.759
where he was sleeping
with the trophy.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:36.829
I really thought I did something
with this MVP trophy, you know,

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.163
and all my friends finally said,

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.365
"Okay, you finally did
something."

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.034
And it was in my hometown
of Chicago,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.301
so that was a great day.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.569
There you go.
You had that going for you.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:44.971
It's really good.
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.640
-I will say, um, I hope
this doesn't hurt your feelings,

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:51.577
but, you know, when you win
an NBA championship trophy,

00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:52.578
everybody's watching.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.013
I want to note in this photo,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.015
every single person
has their back turned.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.184
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.620
Really, nobody cared at all.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.121
-Nobody cared but me.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.424
-Nobody wants to photobomb this.
Nobody wants to be near it.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.526
-Nobody cared but me,
but yeah.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.095
-It's like they're
embarrassed for you.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.596
They're like, "Common's
going to take a picture."

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.131
They're like,
"I don't want to see this."

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.532
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.968
-And they like...
I'm really celebrating,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.471
like I did something,
and they don't give a damn.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.139
-Do you feel like when you're
playing in one of those games --

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:22.108
be honest.
I would imagine you feel

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.510
like the path to the MVP
is putting up points, right?

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.379
It's not an assist situation.
-Right.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.581
-Were you a pretty --
did you share the ball?

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.383
-Well, I was.
I'm like...

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:33.386
I play point guard,
so I'm a good play-maker.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.788
And, you know, unfortunately
in those games

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.056
you just got to score,
score, score.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.591
-Yeah.
-I scored.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.060
But I also was getting a lot
of great assists and rebounds.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.630
I just had an all-around game
kind of like LeBron-ish or...

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.897
-Yeah, sure.
-You know, like,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.632
kind of, you know, all around.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.200
-Your humility is
coming through here.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.535
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.270
-And then we rise, you know?

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.938
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.274
-This is something
that really is cool.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.210
It was the 50th anniversary
of hip-hop last year.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.712
And what an amazing
50 years it's been.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.180
And I think the coolest thing

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.749
about when the 50th anniversary
landed is, you know,

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.618
obviously, like, every--
it's an art form now, right?

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:06.853
Everybody respects it.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.621
It was sort of this
breakthrough format.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.957
And you guys did a concert at
the Vice President's residence.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:14.227
-Yes.
-And what...

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:16.161
It must have been so crazy
to be in D.C.,

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:19.665
to be at the Vice President's
home, doing hip-hop.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.835
-Man, it's times I'm performing

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.137
and I'm like, "Man,
I would have never known

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:27.907
that hip-hop would get me
to this place."

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.976
We celebrated hip-hop 50 years.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.711
It's amazing to celebrate how
powerful this culture has been.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:34.547
It's brought together
so many people,

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.949
but it's been the voice of us
for a long time,

00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:39.518
and it's continuing to be
and so influential.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:41.421
I was so surprised
and loved

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.423
that the Vice President,
she really loved hip-hop,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.926
but she really loved
her hometown hero.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.294
His name is Too Short.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.496
Now, if you all know,
Too Short raps real nasty,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:54.300
but she like,
"But he's one of the greats."

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.701
But the Vice President loved it.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.004
So, I was like, "Man,
this is cool that she..."

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.239
She respected the whole spectrum
of hip-hop,

00:04:00.305 --> 00:04:02.975
not only Too Short,
but Doug E. Fresh, D-Nice,

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.144
myself, Rapsody.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.713
It was a lot of just different
spectrums of artists

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.014
and celebrating hip-hop.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.383
-And are you working
on new music?

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:11.984
Is that something
that's in the future?

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.820
-I'm working on a new album
with the legendary Pete Rock

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:18.824
as the producer,
and man, it's that...

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.126
-Recognition.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.194
[ Applause ]
-I'm so -- I'm so...

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.764
I'm so enthused and inspired
about this project.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:27.533
And, Seth, I'm already plugging

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.003
and saying, "Can I come back
and perform some of this music?"

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.338
-Look, I'm going to run it
up the flagpole.

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:33.806
I'm going to see
what people say.

00:04:33.872 --> 00:04:35.341
No, I would love
to have you back!

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.343
-Oh, man!
-The LeBron James of rap?

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:39.111
Yeah, man.
-Let's go, let's go.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.346
-You guys, right here,
give it up for Common.

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:42.882
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.118
Here we go. "And Then We Rise."
It's on sale now.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.986
We'll be right back
with Tom Hollander.

